# Carried in: 669 Sunken Treasure (Booty Bay), 1116 Dream Dust in the Swamp (Swamp, then Booty Bay),
# 698 Lack of Surplus (flanks done, Tok'Kar), 712 Study of the Elements: Rock (Badlands), 1418 Neeka Bloodscar (Kargath),
# 584 Bloodscalp Clan Heads and 598 Split Bone Necklace (Grom'gol, accepted in segment 13).
# 507 Lord Aliden Perenolde is taken from Krusk in Tarren Mill here (segment 11 leaves it with him).
# Kept for later segments: 1137 and 1183 (Shimmering Flats), 1953 (Tabetha), 1261 (Brackenwall).
# Order: Stonard -> Kargath (grind to 40, 712, 782) -> Undercity/Brill mount -> Alterac -> hearth Stonard (coast quests mounted)
# -> Grom'gol -> Booty Bay -> central Stranglethorn -> Grom'gol/Nesingwary -> hearth Booty Bay.
# Overrides below fix auto data that puts Badlands NPCs in "Outland" and Swamp NPCs in "Zephras Isle".
# Skipped on purpose: 571/573 (rare gorilla drop, then more Grom'gol trips), the elite 793, 197 and 613, and 670/667 (Arathi).

# --- Badlands: grind to 40, Lotwil's bracers and Broken Alliances ---
FLY Kargath | Breyk, Stonard's wind rider master. Leave the Stonard coast quests for now: their mobs are level 41-45 and you come back at 40 with a mount. Your hearthstone stays set to Stonard
T 1418 @ Badlands, 6.5, 47.2 | Neeka Bloodscar in Kargath
A 1420 @ Badlands, 6.5, 47.2 | Neeka. Keep her report until you hearth back to Stonard
L 40 @ Badlands, 14.5, 35.0 | Rock Elementals (39-40) on the slopes north-east of Kargath, then the Lesser Rock Elementals (37-39) along the way east toward Lotwil's camp. They hit hard but have no ranged attacks: Frostbolt, Frost Nova, step back. If they are thin or taken, TUGs' bigger Rock Elemental spot is in the south around 41,79: ride back to Kargath once you are 40
A 782 @ Badlands, 2.9, 45.6 | Gorn in Kargath, now that you are 40
C 712 @ Badlands, 4.1, 79.6 | Greater Rock Elementals (42-44) in the far south-west corner of the Badlands drop Bracers of Rock Binding on most kills. Pull one at a time and kite it. The Dustbelcher ogre camp (Camp Boff) sits right between this group and a second one to the south-east, so pull from the edges and do not drift into the ogres. Kill Boss Tho'grun (next step) if he walks past
C 782 @ Badlands, 12.6, 75.5 | Boss Tho'grun (41-42, not elite) starts at Camp Boff and walks a long loop east along the southern road and back. Catch him on the road, away from the Maulers and Shamans (41-43) in the camp, and loot the Sign of the Earth
T 712 @ Badlands, 25.9, 44.9 | Lotwil Veriatus at his camp in western Badlands
N Optional, Auction House only: with Frost Oil and a Gyrochronatom, Lotwil gives 713 and 714, and only after 714 does 734 -> 777 -> 778 (Fam'retor Guardian) open. Lucien Tosselwrench beside him gives 715 (a Healing Potion and a Lesser Invisibility Potion) and 716 (Patterned Bronze Bracers). Without those items, skip all of them
T 782 @ Badlands, 2.9, 45.6 | Gorn, back in Kargath. Skip the next part (793, elite)

# --- Undercity, Brill and the mount ---
N Teleport: Undercity | No Teleport yet? Fly from Kargath to Undercity instead (your hearthstone is set to Stonard)
TRAIN | Undercity Magic Quarter: learn your level 40 spells
G Tirisfal Glades, 60.0, 52.6 | Leave Undercity and walk north up the road to Brill. Velma Warnam (riding) and Zachariah Post (horses) stand together just west of the inn
N Learn riding from Velma Warnam and buy a skeletal horse from Zachariah Post (Classic: roughly 90-100g for both). Not enough gold? Skip it, keep going on foot and buy it on a later Undercity visit
FLY Tarren Mill | Ride back into Undercity and take a bat from the flight master

# --- Tarren Mill and northern Alterac ---
A 566 | The WANTED poster in Tarren Mill
A 507 @ Hillsbrad Foothills, 63.2, 20.7 | Krusk. He only offers it if you freed Gol'dir and handed in Blackmoore's Legacy (506) in segment 11. If he has nothing for you, skip the 507 and 508 steps below
C 566 | Ride north from Tarren Mill into Alterac Mountains, up to the Uplands at the north edge of the zone. Baron Vardus (40) stands there with Syndicate guards near him: Polymorph one, kill him and take his head. Keep away from the elite Crushridge ogres in the middle of the zone
C 507 | Perenolde's manor lies west of the Uplands, by the shore of Lordamere Lake. Lord Aliden Perenolde (41) is inside, with Syndicate Assassins and Enforcers (38-40) around the manor. Clear them one pull at a time, then kill him
T 507 | Talk to Elysa, who stands right next to him
A 508 @ Alterac Mountains, 39.3, 14.3 | Elysa gives you Taretha's pendant
T 508 | Back in Tarren Mill: Krusk
T 566 | High Executor Darthalia, beside the poster

# --- Stonard and the Misty Reed coast ---
H Stonard | Hearth back to Stonard (still bound there). Hearthstone on cooldown? Fly Tarren Mill to Stonard
T 1420 @ Swamp of Sorrows, 47.7, 55.2 | Helgrum the Swift, next to the wind rider master
A 1430 @ Swamp of Sorrows, 44.7, 57.2 | Dar in Stonard
N Take any new quests offered in Stonard: Forever added several Swamp quests that have no giver data yet. The logger records them
C 1116 @ Swamp of Sorrows, 62.5, 41.0 | Specks of Dream Dust drop from about 1 in 5 of the green dragonkin east of Stonard: Green Scalebanes and Scalebane Captains here, more of them further east toward the coast. Avoid the Elder Dragonkin (45)
T 698 @ Swamp of Sorrows, 81.3, 81.0 | Ride east to the coast, then south along the beach to Tok'Kar at Misty Reed Post. Kill every Monstrous Crawler (43-44) you pass: their legs for Fresh Meat (1430) drop only rarely
A 699 @ Swamp of Sorrows, 81.3, 81.0 | Tok'Kar
C 699 @ Swamp of Sorrows, 78.0, 97.5 | Sawtooth Snappers in the shallows along the south coast, south of the camp: claws drop on most kills. Two more crawlers walk this shore. Short of snappers? More of them live along the east coast
T 699 @ Swamp of Sorrows, 81.3, 81.0 | Tok'Kar
A 1422
T 1422 | Katar, a few steps away
A 1426 @ Swamp of Sorrows, 83.8, 80.4 | Katar
C 1426 | The few Marsh Murlocs are on the beach just south of the camp, and Inkspewers line the whole south and east coast. Most Flesheaters are on the beach west of the camp around 63,86, the same beach you use for Continued Threat: finish 1426 there and wait for respawns if needed. Pull them away from the groups; Frost Nova and Cone of Cold
T 1426 @ Swamp of Sorrows, 83.8, 80.4 | Katar
A 1427
T 1427 | Tok'Kar
A 1428 @ Swamp of Sorrows, 83.8, 80.4 | Katar
C 1428 | Inkspewers, Flesheaters and Oracles further west along the southern beach. Kill Oracles first: they heal
T 1428 @ Swamp of Sorrows, 83.8, 80.4 | Katar
C 1430 @ Swamp of Sorrows, 93.5, 45.0 | Still short of crawler legs? Ride north along the east beach once more: most Monstrous Crawlers walk there, and they have respawned by now. If the legs still will not drop, give up on 1430 rather than camp the beach
T 1430 @ Swamp of Sorrows, 44.7, 57.2 | Ride back to Stonard: Dar

# --- Grom'gol ---
FLY Grom'gol | Breyk, Stonard's wind rider master
A 572 | Far Seer Mok'thardin. The Jungle Stalkers for it are in central Stranglethorn, later in this segment
C 584 | 584 is already in your log from your last visit. Ruins of Zul'Kunda in the far north-west: Gan'zulah (41) and Nezzliok the Dire (40) stand inside the ruins among Bloodscalp trolls. Clear around each one first, then kill them for their heads
A 196 @ Stranglethorn Vale, 35.7, 10.8 | Hemet Nesingwary, a short ride east of Zul'Kunda at the hunters' camp
T 584 | The Bubbling Cauldron in the middle of Grom'gol
A 585,586 | Both come from the cauldron. They are done in central Stranglethorn after Booty Bay
FLY Booty Bay | Thysta, Grom'gol's wind rider master

